  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skills for Youth Resilience Program (SYRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the Skills for Youth Resilience Programme (SYRP) is to help young people (aged 16-30) in Mozambique and Zimbabwe gain employment or start and develop their own businesses. It will focus on the provision of holistic Technical Vocational and Educational Training (TVET), including entrepreneurship and life skills training, to marginalised young people through support for training centres run by local partners Young Africa in Mozambique and Zimbabwe and Young Africa HUB in Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
